\pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  22. (ff. 288r\endash 320v, 324r\endash 328v, 1. Z.) \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24  Olympiodorus Alexandrinus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , In Platonis Phaedonem commentarium (Ms. \plain \f3\lang1033\fs24 \u8127 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u927 \'cf\u955 \'eb\u965 \'f5\u956 \'ec\u960 \'f0\u953 \'e9\u959 \'ef\u948 \'e4\u8061 ?\u961 \'f1\u959 \'ef\u965 \'f5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [am Rand, s. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  S\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Hand h]\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u7952 ?\u958 \'ee\u8053 ?\u947 \'e3\u951 \'e7\u963 \'f3\u953 \'e9\u962 \'f2 \u963 \'f3\u959 \'ef\u966 \'f6\u969 \'f9\u964 \'f4\u8049 ?\u964 \'f4\u951 \'e7 \u949 \'e5\u7984 ?\u962 \'f2 \u964 \'f4\u8056 ?\u957 \'ed \u928 \'d0\u955 \'eb\u8049 ?\u964 \'f4\u969 \'f9\u957 \'ed\u959 \'ef\u962 \'f2 \u948 \'e4\u953 \'e9\u8049 ?\u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u947 \'e3\u959 \'ef\u957 \'ed \u960 \'f0\u949 \'e5\u961 \'f1\u8054 ? \u7936 ?\u952 \'e8\u945 \'e1\u957 \'ed\u945 \'e1\u963 \'f3\u8055 ?\u945 \'e1\u962 \'f2 \u964 \'f4\u8134 ?\u962 \'f2 \u968 \'f8\u965 \'f5\u967 \'f7\u8134 ?\u962 \'f2\u903 ? \u7952 ?\u963 \'f3\u964 \'f4\u8054 ? \u948 \'e4\u8050 ? \u7936 ?\u954 \'ea\u8051 ?\u966 \'f6\u945 \'e1\u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  inc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8249 \'8b\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u917 \'c5\u7984 ?\u960 \'f0\u8060 ?\u957 \'ed \plain \f6\lang1033\fs24 \u8001 ? \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u931 \'d3\u969 \'f9\u954 \'ea\u961 \'f1\u8049 ?\u964 \'f4\u951 \'e7\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8250 \'9b, \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u8005 ?\u964 \'f4\u953 \'e9, \u949 \'e5\u7984 ? \u966 \'f6\u953 \'e9\u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u963 \'f3\u959 \'ef\u966 \'f6\u949 \'e5\u8150 ? \plain \f6\lang1033\fs24 \u8001 ? \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u917 \'c5\u8016 ?\u951 \'e7\u957 \'ed\u8057 ?\u962 \'f2 \u954 \'ea\u964 \'f4\u955 \'eb.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , ed. L. G. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Westerink\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , The Greek Commentaries on Plato\rquote s Phaedo, I. Olympiodorus, Dilton Marsh Westbury \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  2009, S. 39\endash 181; ed. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Norvin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Lit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ), S. 1\endash 83 (= A I 1\endash A XIII 20). (f. 320v) Randnotiz des Schreibers in Rot bez\u252 \'fcglich des l\u252 \'fcckenhaften Textes, s. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  S\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash (ff. 321r\endash 323v) leer, um die Textl\u252 \'fccke anzuzeigen, s. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Westerink\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , The Greek Commentaries, I, S. 165 (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  app. crit.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). Weitere kurzere Textauslassungen, an diesen Stellen Zeilen ganz oder teilweise leer gelassen (ff. 318v, 319r). \endash Kommentartext von den Lemmata gelegentlich durch Trennzeichen und eine kurze Textl\u252 \'fccke abgesetzt.}

